                <pb facs="0812" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg714"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Léger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Haiti</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-09-15"><hi rendition="#italic">September 15,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: I hasten to inform you
                    that I have returned to Washington. I was sorry to hear, on my landing at New
                    York, the sorrowful news of the Galveston disaster. Permit me to join in the
                    mourning of so many distressed families and to lament with you the losses that
                    the country has just sustained.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. N. Léger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
